WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.017
Here is the Shuttle board, and what each of its buttons does.

2
00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:12.801
The Desk sorts tasks into three lanes: drafts not yet started, work in flight, and results awaiting your review.

3
00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:17.070
To write a task yourself, click the plus on Drafts.

4
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:23.828
The Stash form asks for a title, optional details, a project and an agent.

5
00:00:23.978 --> 00:00:27.702
One-shot is a single task. Standing repeats on a schedule.

6
00:00:27.852 --> 00:00:30.383
Stash saves it as a draft card.

7
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.024
Or click the star on In flight, and describe an idea in your own words.

8
00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:39.376
Pick a project and press Spawn.

9
00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:43.713
An agent turns your words into a task, and its card appears a moment later.

10
00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:47.024
Click any card to open it.

11
00:00:47.174 --> 00:00:51.988
The strip under its title, showing who works it and where, unfolds its actions.

12
00:00:52.138 --> 00:00:56.113
Write a message for the worker if you like, then choose how to send it.

13
00:00:56.263 --> 00:01:00.993
New session starts a fresh conversation, which reads the task and its notes from the top.

14
00:01:01.143 --> 00:01:05.132
If a worker is still running, the board asks before cutting it off.

15
00:01:05.282 --> 00:01:09.608
Resume picks up the task’s last conversation, with everything it remembered.

16
00:01:09.758 --> 00:01:12.519
Use it when finished work needs one more change.

17
00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:16.999
Meeting records a conversation and joins it to this task.

18
00:01:17.149 --> 00:01:25.023
Call records this computer’s microphone and system audio. Room uses its microphone alone. Phone streams a phone’s microphone through the board.

19
00:01:25.173 --> 00:01:30.498
The worker follows the live transcript, takes notes, and answers when you address it by name.

20
00:01:30.648 --> 00:01:32.360
Stop ends the recording.

21
00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:39.779
On a running card, Aloft opens the worker’s conversation, in a terminal, a browser, or a desktop app.

22
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.433
When a worker finishes, its outcome waits here for you.

23
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:49.355
Read it, then press Temper to accept the result, or Discard to set it aside.

24
00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:55.149
To try it, set up Shuttle on one machine, and start with one small task.
